 ### Error responses
 
-FCM returns `200 OK` even when delivery fails — servers MUST always check the response
-body:
+The FCM HTTP v1 API answers a failed send with an HTTP error status and a body whose
+`error.status` is the general Google API status (`NOT_FOUND`, `PERMISSION_DENIED`, ...).
+The FCM-specific code is the `errorCode` of the `error.details` entry whose `@type` is
+`type.googleapis.com/google.firebase.fcm.v1.FcmError`; servers MUST read it there, and
+SHOULD fall back to `error.status` only when no such entry is present. A body carrying
+`error` is a failure whatever the HTTP status.
 
